    "id": "prop:published-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "In the special case \\(q=0\\) and \\(H=1\\), with the corresponding one-date Choi--Yuan subgroup conditions, \\(B_2=o(s)\\), the third overlap score is absorbed at their pointwise scale, and the standardized leading score and variance reduce to the group central limit theorem and variance formula in Choi and Yuan (2024), Theorem 3.1.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "q",
      "H",
      "Btwo",
      "s"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "lem:complete-tangent",
      "def:complete-tangent-score",
      "def:quadratic-drift",
      "def:oracle-score-variance",
      "lem:one-date-curvature-overlap",
      "lem:choi-yuan-one-date-group-clt"
    ],
    "justification": "The reduction guards against changing the estimand or estimator while enlarging the dependence and target regimes.",
    "gap": "The published theorem is the reduction target rather than an unresolved result.",
    "consumer": "Applied users recover the existing one-date procedure when no serial or window correction is needed.",
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(q=0\\), \\(H=1\\), and \\(W=\\{t_0\\}\\).  Average the complete tangent identity over \\(i\\in G\\).  With \\(\\bar x_G=g^{-1}\\sum_{i\\in G}x_i\\), \\(A=A_{t_0}\\), and \\(B=B_S\\), this gives the exact decomposition\n\\[\n L=\\mathcal D_n+\\mathcal T_n-\\mathcal O_n,\n\\]\nwhere\n\\[\n \\mathcal D_n=\\sum_{j\\in C(t_0)}\\bar x_G^\\top A^{-1}x_j\\epsilon_{j,t_0},\n \\qquad\n \\mathcal T_n=\\frac1g\\sum_{i\\in G}\\sum_{u\\in S}\n f_{t_0}^\\top B^{-1}f_u\\epsilon_{iu},\n\\]\nand \\(\\mathcal O_n\\) is the donor--pretreatment overlap score defined in the one-date curvature lemma.  That lemma proves both\n\\[\n \\mathcal O_n=o_{\\mathbb P}(s),\n \\qquad B_2=o_{\\mathbb P}(s).\n\\]\n\nWhen \\(q=0\\), the coordinates entering \\(\\mathcal D_n\\), \\(\\mathcal T_n\\), and \\(\\mathcal O_n\\) are pairwise disjoint and conditionally independent.  Therefore the variance of the two-term leading score is\n\\[\n V_{\\mathrm{CY}}\n =\\operatorname{Var}(\\mathcal D_n+\\mathcal T_n\\mid M,\\Omega)\n =\\gamma(0)\\left\\{\n   \\bar x_G^\\top A^{-1}\\bar x_G\n   +\\frac1g f_{t_0}^\\top B^{-1}f_{t_0}\n \\right\\}.\n\\]\nMoreover,\n\\[\n s^2=V_{\\mathrm{CY}}+\\operatorname{Var}(\\mathcal O_n\\mid M,\\Omega),\n \\qquad\n \\frac{\\operatorname{Var}(\\mathcal O_n\\mid M,\\Omega)}{s^2}=o(1),\n\\]\nso \\(V_{\\mathrm{CY}}/s^2\\to1\\).\n\nThe variance is invariant to the scaling used for the singular factors.  Indeed, because \\(x_j=D^{1/2}U_{j\\cdot}^\\top\\) and \\(f_u=D^{1/2}V_{u\\cdot}^\\top\\),\n\\[\n \\bar x_G^\\top A^{-1}\\bar x_G\n =\\bar U_G^\\top\n   \\left(\\sum_{j\\in C(t_0)}U_{j\\cdot}^\\top U_{j\\cdot}\\right)^{-1}\n   \\bar U_G,\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n f_{t_0}^\\top B^{-1}f_{t_0}\n =V_{t_0\\cdot}\n   \\left(\\sum_{u\\in S}V_{u\\cdot}^\\top V_{u\\cdot}\\right)^{-1}\n   V_{t_0\\cdot}^\\top.\n\\]\nThese are exactly the donor-loading and group-size-scaled pretreatment-factor quadratic forms displayed in Choi and Yuan (2024), Theorem 3.1.  The cited theorem supplies the published one-date group central limit theorem under its stated conditions.  The identities above show that the first two components of the complete score and their variance are its leading score and variance, while the established \\(o_{\\mathbb P}(s)\\) bound shows that the donor--pretreatment overlap is absorbed at that scale.  Together with \\(B_2=o_{\\mathbb P}(s)\\), this proves the claimed reduction.",
